00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:17.180
And then you said you saw the performances by Steve and Amy.

255
00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:20.260
And you're like, of course they have to say I love you.

256
00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:21.960
Were you worried about that?

257
00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:23.640
Like, how serious was that conversation?

258
00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:29.290
Well, so interesting that you prepared by listening to the commentary, which I should

259
00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:31.890
have done because I have no memory of that or saying that.

260
00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:35.390
I think the performances were great in this.

261
00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:41.650
And, you know, there's a number of moments where I thought, oh, well, this is the whole

262
00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:41.990
point.

263
00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:47.650
And, you know, I feel like this, the episode is very Paul Lieberstein to me in a way,

264
00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:52.970
because he's a very subtle writer and, like, important things happen, but on the surface,

265
00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:54.330
they're small things.

266
00:11:54.450 --> 00:12:02.010
And he found, and obviously with Padnick, but he found this, you know, this way for it

267
00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:07.910
to be buried in a comedy story for them to say that and to say, do you love me, love me?

268
00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:08.710
I love you, love you.

269
00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.070
That, to me, feels really Paul in my head.

270
00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:17.610
But, and yeah, and Amy's amazing, Amy Ryan, the way she flushed and everything.

271
00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:24.550
And there's, like, a really big romantic story point in the middle of this episode that seems

272
00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:28.070
like it's just about PDAs and everything, but it is a big advancement for them.

273
00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:32.410
But it's also episode 16 of season seven, and Steve leaves, like, episode 20.

274
00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:36.350
So, you know, you got to roll it along.

275
00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:38.750
Yeah, I think that was you guys' worry.

276
00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:43.490
It sounded like that if, well, if they say this here, what does that mean for the next,

277
00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:44.630
